course: dictionary
lesson: 3043
title: Earthquake: a sudden shaking of the ground
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: An earthquake is a sudden, violent shaking of the ground. It happens when rocks deep inside the Earth move. Sudden means it comes all at once, without warning, and violent means very strong.
explain: Read this: «In an earthquake drill you drop, cover under a desk and hold on, because falling objects cause most injuries.» The words drill, drop, cover and falling are clues. The ground is shaking hard, so things can fall.
explain: Earthquake is a noun, a word for a thing. You can have a strong earthquake, a big earthquake or many earthquakes. Look inside the word: earth and quake, a quake being a shaking of the Earth.
fact: An earthquake is a sudden, violent shaking of the ground.
fact: Earthquakes are caused by movement of rocks deep inside the Earth.
fact: The Earth's outer shell is made of huge plates; when they slip past each other, the ground shakes.
fact: Earthquakes are common in places like California, Japan, New Zealand and around the Pacific "Ring of Fire".
fact: In an earthquake, use Drop, Cover and Hold On, and stay away from windows.
exercise: «The 2004 Indian Ocean tsunami, after a magnitude 9.1 earthquake off Sumatra, killed about 230,000 people.» What does earthquake mean here? | A type of wave made by the wind | A map of the seabed | A quiet swim in the sea | *A sudden, violent shaking of the ground
exercise: In an earthquake drill, what should you do? | Run outside as fast as you can | Stand next to the windows to watch | *Drop, cover under a desk and hold on | Ring your friends
exercise: What causes an earthquake? | Too many people in one town | Wind blowing through the trees | Rain falling on the roof | *Movement of rocks deep inside the Earth
test: «Nobody can yet predict the exact day of an earthquake, but strong buildings save many lives.» What does this sentence tell us? | Earthquakes only happen at night | We always know the exact day of an earthquake | *We cannot yet know exactly when an earthquake will happen | Strong buildings cause earthquakes
test: «If an earthquake at the coast is long or strong, go to high ground or inland at once, because a tsunami may follow within minutes.» Why should you go to high ground? | Because the sea is warmer on hills | *Because a tsunami may follow within minutes | Because earthquakes are fun to watch from a hill | Because the air is cleaner up there
exam: Which sentence uses earthquake correctly? | An earthquake is a good colour for a bedroom wall | She earthquaked the cake into the bin | We earthquaked our way to the park after school | *The town felt a strong earthquake at breakfast time
